**Files changed:** `src/rust_mv/rust_mv.rs` (created from scratch)

**Behavior implemented:**
- Single-source (`SRC DEST`) and multi-source (`SRC... DIR`) invocation forms
- Effective destination computed as `DIR/basename(SRC)` when the destination is an existing directory
- Option parsing: `--` terminator, bare `-` as filename, unknown options rejected
- Invocation-wide validation (missing operands, unknown options, multi-source target not a directory) before any filesystem modification
- Per-source error handling with continuation; exit status 1 if any source failed
- Core `move_path` function performing the filesystem rename
- Pre-rename detection of: identical source/destination, directory-into-itself (both existing and non-existing destination paths), type incompatibility (file↔dir), non-empty directory merge
- Symlink handling via `symlink_metadata` (lstat) so symlinks are moved as themselves
- Preservation of modes and contents (guaranteed by `rename(2)`)
- Arbitrary non-UTF-8 pathname bytes preserved via `OsString`/`OsStr`/`Path`
- No panics; all errors returned as `Result` and reported on stderr with the affected operand identified
- No flags, no prompts, no cross-filesystem fallback, no parent creation
